<title>USA: USDA ups Ecuador limit under GSM-102 by $18 mln.</title>
<headline>USDA ups Ecuador limit under GSM-102 by $18 mln.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1997-07-22</dateline>
<text>
<p>The U.S. Agriculture Department Tuesday said it raised by $18 million Ecuador's limit for sales of U.S. farm goods to the Andean Region under the Export Credit Guarantee Program (GSM-102) in fiscal 1997.</p>
<p>The total fiscal 1997 authorization for the Andean Region -- Bolivia, Chile, Colombia, Ecuador, Peru and Venezuela -- remains at $350 million, with $200 million  allocated and $150 million unallocated, USDA said.</p>
</text>
